# Close Terminals & Free Ports (Strict)

Closing a terminal pane is **not** enough. Orphan Node/Vite processes from **agent** work often keep listening. Before every final reply, stop what **you** started and free only those ports.

## Ports

| Service | Port |
|---------|------|
| Admin / Vite (`admin/`) | **5173** |

Do **not** leave **5173** occupied after your turn if **you** started anything that bound it. Do **not** free that port if it was already in use by the user. Vite is configured with `strictPort`, so it will not move to another port.

## Prefer External Dev Servers

- The user runs long-lived `npm run dev` in an **external** terminal. Prefer that.
- Follow `reuse-existing-dev-servers`: check listeners first; never auto-start `dev`; never kill a pre-existing listener.
- Do **not** start persistent API/web servers in Cursor integrated terminals unless a short verification requires it **and** the port is free.
- Prefer one-shot checks (`curl`, `npm run build`, `npx tsc`, tests) over keeping `dev` running.

## Required End-of-Turn Checklist

1. Stop every process/job **you** started this chat (dev, watch, background shells).
2. Force-free **5173** **only** when **your** process (or an orphan from this chat) still holds it — never because the user left it listening.
3. Confirm **your** listeners are gone before the final message.
4. Never rely on the user to clean up; never tear down their already-running servers.

## Force-Free Ports (Windows / PowerShell)

Run before ending the turn **only** when agent-started work may still hold 5173:

```powershell
foreach ($port in 5173) {
  Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort $port -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
    Select-Object -ExpandProperty OwningProcess -Unique |
    ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_ -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }
}
```

Fallback if `Get-NetTCPConnection` is unavailable:

```powershell
netstat -ano | findstr ":5173"
# then: Stop-Process -Id <PID> -Force
```

Killing the terminal session PID alone is insufficient when children keep the port.

## Exceptions

- Leave a process running **only** if the user explicitly asks (e.g. "leave the server running").
- Do **not** kill listeners on 5173 that the user already had running in an **external** terminal **unless** you (or an orphan from this chat) are what is holding the port, or the user asked you to free it.
- Do **not** free port **3000** (LevelUP API) unless you started that process in this chat.
- Postgres on **5432** (LevelUP) and **5433** (Induction Docker) is out of scope — do not stop DB containers unless asked.
